:: bucky [trainer]
"Hey, you!" a friendly voice calls. The trainer is standing near the tree, balancing a stack of apples on their head. "Are you ready to have a contest?"

<<linkreplace 'Ask about the contest.' t8n>>\
    "It's an apple balancing contest, of course! Think you can balance more apples on your head than I can?"

    [[Umm, sure.->bucky: apples]]
    [[Another time: Continue exploring Route 001.->b4]]
<</linkreplace>>


:: bucky: apples [contest]
<<set $appleNumber1 to random(4, 10)>>\
<<set $appleNumber2 to random(4, 10)>>\
<<set $appleNumber3 to random(3, 5)>>\
<<set $appleAnswer = ($appleNumber1 + $appleNumber2) * $appleNumber3>>\
"Listen close, my friend." The trainer points to the apples on their head.

"I have $appleNumber1 apples on my head." Their arms move in a flash as they pick more apples from the tree.

"And then I throw $appleNumber2 more apples up on top, like this!" You can't believe that none of them fall as they throw them up and onto their stack.

"I'll tell you a secret about the apples from this tree...they all have $appleNumber3 worms in them. All of them! It's weird, right? And that's why I don't eat these. Worms are friends.

"Here is your challenge. How many little friends do I have on my head right now?"

<<numberbox "$appleGuess" 0 autofocus>>
[[Give your answer.->bucky: apple result]]

:: bucky: apple result [contest]
<<if $appleAnswer == $appleGuess>>\
	"Correct! You win!" With a shake of their head all the apples come tumbling down.

    They catch one in their hand and toss it your way. You put it away and now you have $appleNumber3 little friends in your bag, quietly munching away on the apple.
<<else>>\
    "So close! But not the right answer. Try again."

    Hint: The problem is ($appleNumber1 + $appleNumber2) and multiply by $appleNumber3.
    <<numberbox "$appleGuess" 0 autofocus>>
    [[Give your answer.->bucky: apple result]]
<</if>>
[[Continue exploring.->b4]]